{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"docs-preset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Docs Preset"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The docs preset composes the built-in callout, comment-component, component-transform, and heading-collection extensions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\nimport { docsMarkdownExtensions } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs'\n\nconst extensions = docsMarkdownExtensions()\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source, { extensions })\nconst html = renderHtml(document, {\n  extensions,\n  headingAnchors: true,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The preset is a separate 2.3 KB gzip entry and is not imported by the parser or renderers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"callouts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callouts"}]},{"type":"code","value":"> [!TIP] Cache the parsed document\n> Rendering an AST avoids parsing the same article again.","lang":"md"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This produces a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CalloutNode"},{"type":"text","value":" and renders "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markdown-alert"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markdown-alert-title"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markdown-alert-content"},{"type":"text","value":" classes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep blank lines inside a callout quoted with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":">"},{"type":"text","value":". An unquoted blank line ends the callout. Custom titles are plain text; put Markdown links in the body."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"heading-collection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heading collection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heading collection adds table-of-contents data to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.headings"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const document = parseMarkdown('# Guide\\n\\n## Install', {\n  extensions: docsMarkdownExtensions(),\n})\n\ndocument.headings\n// [\n//   { id: 'guide', text: 'Guide', level: 1 },\n//   { id: 'install', text: 'Install', level: 2 },\n// ]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable collection with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"docsMarkdownExtensions({ collectHeadings: false })"},{"type":"text","value":", or configure component names that should not contribute headings."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"comment-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comment components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single components use one HTML comment:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- ::separator tone=\"subtle\" -->","lang":"md"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Block components use matching start and end comments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- ::start:tabs -->\n\n## React\n\nReact content\n\n## Solid\n\nSolid content\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->","lang":"md"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Names are normalized to lowercase. Quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes are supported."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tab-variants","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tab variants"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The preset transforms these "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabs"},{"type":"text","value":" variants:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output metadata"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sections divided by the shallowest heading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tab names, slugs, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"md-tab-panel"},{"type":"text","value":" children"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"files"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fenced code blocks with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file="},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title="}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"file metadata and one panel per file"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package-manager"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package..."},{"type":"text","value":" lines or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework: package..."},{"type":"text","value":" lines"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package groups and install mode"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bundler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite and Rsbuild heading sections"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"available bundlers and panel content"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The transforms emit custom element names and JSON "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-*"},{"type":"text","value":" properties. Your application owns the components and behavior attached to that contract."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package-manager lines without a framework prefix apply to every framework. Each line is a separate command, so this block supplies three commands to the application's package-manager component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list\n@tanstack/intent@latest validate\n@tanstack/intent@latest review\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->","lang":"md"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A line is a framework line when it starts with a name made of letters, digits, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by a colon, so both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react:package"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react: package"},{"type":"text","value":" select the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react"},{"type":"text","value":" group. A colon that starts a URL or path does not begin a framework prefix: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://example.com/package.tgz"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file:../local-package"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git+ssh://"},{"type":"text","value":" specifiers are shared commands. A framework line can still install a protocol package, as in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react: file:../local-package"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-package-manager-meta"},{"type":"text","value":" JSON keeps shared commands under the empty string key in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packagesByFramework"},{"type":"text","value":". This fallback group comes first. Named framework groups include shared lines in source order, so renderers can select a named group or fall back to the shared group. Framework discovery should ignore the empty key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a fenced text block inside the component when command arguments contain literal Markdown characters such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<package>#<skill>"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"framework-panels","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework panels"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":" blocks split top-level framework headings into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"md-framework-panel"},{"type":"text","value":" elements. Nested headings receive a framework label, while top-level selector headings are omitted from collected table-of-contents data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the individual "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/extensions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extension entry points"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when the complete preset is more than your site needs."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"docs-preset","text":"Docs Preset","level":1},{"id":"callouts","text":"Callouts","level":2},{"id":"heading-collection","text":"Heading collection","level":2},{"id":"comment-components","text":"Comment components","level":2},{"id":"tab-variants","text":"Tab variants","level":2},{"id":"framework-panels","text":"Framework panels","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Docs Preset\n\nThe docs preset composes the built-in callout, comment-component, component-transform, and heading-collection extensions.\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\nimport { docsMarkdownExtensions } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs'\n\nconst extensions = docsMarkdownExtensions()\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source, { extensions })\nconst html = renderHtml(document, {\n  extensions,\n  headingAnchors: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe preset is a separate 2.3 KB gzip entry and is not imported by the parser or renderers.\n\n## Callouts\n\n```md\n> [!TIP] Cache the parsed document\n> Rendering an AST avoids parsing the same article again.\n```\n\nThis produces a `CalloutNode` and renders `markdown-alert`, `markdown-alert-title`, and `markdown-alert-content` classes.\n\nKeep blank lines inside a callout quoted with `>`. An unquoted blank line ends the callout. Custom titles are plain text; put Markdown links in the body.\n\n## Heading collection\n\nHeading collection adds table-of-contents data to `document.headings`:\n\n```ts\nconst document = parseMarkdown('# Guide\\n\\n## Install', {\n  extensions: docsMarkdownExtensions(),\n})\n\ndocument.headings\n// [\n//   { id: 'guide', text: 'Guide', level: 1 },\n//   { id: 'install', text: 'Install', level: 2 },\n// ]\n```\n\nDisable collection with `docsMarkdownExtensions({ collectHeadings: false })`, or configure component names that should not contribute headings.\n\n## Comment components\n\nSingle components use one HTML comment:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::separator tone=\"subtle\" -->\n```\n\nBlock components use matching start and end comments:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::start:tabs -->\n\n## React\n\nReact content\n\n## Solid\n\nSolid content\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n```\n\nNames are normalized to lowercase. Quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes are supported.\n\n## Tab variants\n\nThe preset transforms these `tabs` variants:\n\n| Variant | Input model | Output metadata |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| default | Sections divided by the shallowest heading | tab names, slugs, and `md-tab-panel` children |\n| `files` | Fenced code blocks with `file=` or `title=` | file metadata and one panel per file |\n| `package-manager` | Shared `package...` lines or `framework: package...` lines | package groups and install mode |\n| `bundler` | Vite and Rsbuild heading sections | available bundlers and panel content |\n\nThe transforms emit custom element names and JSON `data-*` properties. Your application owns the components and behavior attached to that contract.\n\nPackage-manager lines without a framework prefix apply to every framework. Each line is a separate command, so this block supplies three commands to the application's package-manager component:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list\n@tanstack/intent@latest validate\n@tanstack/intent@latest review\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n```\n\nA line is a framework line when it starts with a name made of letters, digits, `_`, or `-` followed by a colon, so both `react:package` and `react: package` select the `react` group. A colon that starts a URL or path does not begin a framework prefix: `https://example.com/package.tgz`, `file:../local-package`, and `git+ssh://` specifiers are shared commands. A framework line can still install a protocol package, as in `react: file:../local-package`.\n\nThe `data-package-manager-meta` JSON keeps shared commands under the empty string key in `packagesByFramework`. This fallback group comes first. Named framework groups include shared lines in source order, so renderers can select a named group or fall back to the shared group. Framework discovery should ignore the empty key.\n\nUse a fenced text block inside the component when command arguments contain literal Markdown characters such as `<package>#<skill>` or `*`.\n\n## Framework panels\n\n`framework` blocks split top-level framework headings into `md-framework-panel` elements. Nested headings receive a framework label, while top-level selector headings are omitted from collected table-of-contents data.\n\nUse the individual [extension entry points](../reference/extensions.md) when the complete preset is more than your site needs.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Docs Preset\n---\n\n# Docs Preset\n\nThe docs preset composes the built-in callout, comment-component, component-transform, and heading-collection extensions.\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { renderHtml } from '@tanstack/markdown/html'\nimport { docsMarkdownExtensions } from '@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs'\n\nconst extensions = docsMarkdownExtensions()\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source, { extensions })\nconst html = renderHtml(document, {\n  extensions,\n  headingAnchors: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe preset is a separate 2.3 KB gzip entry and is not imported by the parser or renderers.\n\n## Callouts\n\n```md\n> [!TIP] Cache the parsed document\n> Rendering an AST avoids parsing the same article again.\n```\n\nThis produces a `CalloutNode` and renders `markdown-alert`, `markdown-alert-title`, and `markdown-alert-content` classes.\n\nKeep blank lines inside a callout quoted with `>`. An unquoted blank line ends the callout. Custom titles are plain text; put Markdown links in the body.\n\n## Heading collection\n\nHeading collection adds table-of-contents data to `document.headings`:\n\n```ts\nconst document = parseMarkdown('# Guide\\n\\n## Install', {\n  extensions: docsMarkdownExtensions(),\n})\n\ndocument.headings\n// [\n//   { id: 'guide', text: 'Guide', level: 1 },\n//   { id: 'install', text: 'Install', level: 2 },\n// ]\n```\n\nDisable collection with `docsMarkdownExtensions({ collectHeadings: false })`, or configure component names that should not contribute headings.\n\n## Comment components\n\nSingle components use one HTML comment:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::separator tone=\"subtle\" -->\n```\n\nBlock components use matching start and end comments:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::start:tabs -->\n\n## React\n\nReact content\n\n## Solid\n\nSolid content\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n```\n\nNames are normalized to lowercase. Quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes are supported.\n\n## Tab variants\n\nThe preset transforms these `tabs` variants:\n\n| Variant | Input model | Output metadata |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| default | Sections divided by the shallowest heading | tab names, slugs, and `md-tab-panel` children |\n| `files` | Fenced code blocks with `file=` or `title=` | file metadata and one panel per file |\n| `package-manager` | Shared `package...` lines or `framework: package...` lines | package groups and install mode |\n| `bundler` | Vite and Rsbuild heading sections | available bundlers and panel content |\n\nThe transforms emit custom element names and JSON `data-*` properties. Your application owns the components and behavior attached to that contract.\n\nPackage-manager lines without a framework prefix apply to every framework. Each line is a separate command, so this block supplies three commands to the application's package-manager component:\n\n```md\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list\n@tanstack/intent@latest validate\n@tanstack/intent@latest review\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n```\n\nA line is a framework line when it starts with a name made of letters, digits, `_`, or `-` followed by a colon, so both `react:package` and `react: package` select the `react` group. A colon that starts a URL or path does not begin a framework prefix: `https://example.com/package.tgz`, `file:../local-package`, and `git+ssh://` specifiers are shared commands. A framework line can still install a protocol package, as in `react: file:../local-package`.\n\nThe `data-package-manager-meta` JSON keeps shared commands under the empty string key in `packagesByFramework`. This fallback group comes first. Named framework groups include shared lines in source order, so renderers can select a named group or fall back to the shared group. Framework discovery should ignore the empty key.\n\nUse a fenced text block inside the component when command arguments contain literal Markdown characters such as `<package>#<skill>` or `*`.\n\n## Framework panels\n\n`framework` blocks split top-level framework headings into `md-framework-panel` elements. Nested headings receive a framework label, while top-level selector headings are omitted from collected table-of-contents data.\n\nUse the individual [extension entry points](../reference/extensions.md) when the complete preset is more than your site needs.\n"}
